[38;5;231m⏺[39m Approved — noting we're on the architectural path, so "go ahead" takes us to the spec and then an implementation plan,
  not straight to code. Redirect me if you actually want me implementing now.

  One thing I owe you before writing the spec. This repo has no lint config, no formatter, no test script, and no CI —
  and setting any of it up is cheapest right now, before the logger exists, because whatever you pick becomes the
  standard the logger is written to rather than something retrofitted onto it.

  Relevant to this change specifically: the redaction scrub and the level-threshold comparison are exactly the kind of
  logic that's wrong in a way review doesn't catch — a denylist that misses nested objects, an off-by-one on the level
  filter. Those are cheap unit tests and expensive production surprises. Node's built-in [38;5;153mnode:test[39m runner needs no
  dependencies, which keeps the zero-dependency stance you picked in the module-format fork; ESLint and Prettier would
  be the repo's first [38;5;153mdevDependencies[39m and its first lockfile.

